;;; A `(query :goal …)` whose relation head is a variable.
;;;
;;; Two lines, and the shortest find the fuzzer has produced. `(?R Rex
;;; Animal)` is the same shape the loader refuses inside a rule — a rule
;;; compiles once per activator (Q29), so a head variable must be bound by
;;; one — and a *query* goal has no activator at all, so it can never be
;;; bound. A query's `:goal` is held to what a rule's `:match` is held to
;;; (Q-M1f.72), so the program is refused at load, on every command, exit 1:
;;;
;;;     kb load error: query: its :goal writes (?R Rex Animal) with ?R as its
;;;     relation, which nothing binds — a relation is named by a name, or by a
;;;     rule's parameter its activator binds, and a query has no activator
;;;
;;; The wrong answer it witnesses: no bindings, and "(no query goal to
;;; project)", running a program that should have been refused; an engine
;;; that compiled the goal only where a model is rendered printed
;;; `ein.inference.compile.CompileError: unbound relation head ?R …` there.
;;;
;;; `query-goal-free-head-unsat.ein` is the sibling whose puzzle is
;;; contradictory, refused the same way.
;;;
;;;

(is-a Rex Animal)

(query
  :goal (?R Rex Animal))
